--- final message ---
`paper.tex`, `claims_grounding.json` and `figure_manifest.json` are written, and the paper compiles to `paper.pdf`. The `compile_latex.sh` and `validate_figures.py` checks could not run in this workspace.

**Paper:** the frozen five-statistic ridge predictor against the 2m(n−1) bound and two controls, on the sealed final evaluation.

| Predictor | Family-macro log MAE |
|---|---|
| Five-statistic ridge | 0.181 |
| Constant (training geometric mean) | 0.870 |
| Ridge scored against shuffled targets | 1.423 |
| 2m(n−1) bound | 1.754 |

- **Noise and outcome:** the median relative Monte Carlo standard error of the labels is 0.029. The final outcome is `qualified` and `completed`, and the paper says so.
- **No improvement claim:** the selected configuration is the seed baseline and the search found no winner, so the paper makes no improvement claim. The search score (−0.1913) is kept in the Supplementary Information, apart from the final metrics.
- **Open question:** per-family errors were not retained, so the "which graph types fail" half of the research question is stated as unknown.
- **Unscored variant:** the unscored Matthews/resistance variant appears only as untested future work.
- **Added analysis:** exact log overshoot of the bound on path, cycle, star and complete graphs (closed forms, checked against exact enumeration at n=7). It also includes a label-noise estimate under a Gaussian assumption and a worst-case bound on how concentrated the error can be. It does not use per-family data.
- **Layout:** the body is 8 pages, references are on page 9, and the Supplementary Information is on pages 10–11. The ICLR double-blind format is kept, with "Anonymous authors" and an LLM-usage subsection in the SI.

**Validation**
- The claims validator passes with 17 grounded claims.
- The evidence verifier reports zero dangling references.

**Not validated**
- **Compile script:** it needs `pdftotext`, which is not installed. I compiled with `pdflatex` and `bibtex` directly.
- **Figure validator:** it needs the `src` package, which is absent.
- **Overview figure:** `figures/overview_pipeline.png` is a placeholder; the orchestrator renders the real one. It will be taller, so the body may spill onto a ninth page.
- **Closed-form claims:** these are backed by `closed_form_gap.json` through evidence refs. They are not in `claims_grounding.json`, because `paper_data.json` has no source id for them.
- **Protocol facts:** the train/test counts, the family list and the 300-walk figure came from copies of the task resources in `protocol_inputs/`. They are not from `paper_data.json`.

**References:** the paper cites only the three entries in `references.bib` (two Feige papers and Kiwi et al.). Aleliunas et al. and Lovász are named in the text without citations, since they are not in the bibliography.
